  "evidence": "70 raw hardware CSV objects byte-verified by Git blob IDs, with SHA-256 for independent replay. Seven experimental groups; no inference of statistical independence across rows.",
  "semantics": "Acrobot uses active joint 2, Pendubot active joint 1. tau_con records the controller-output history. tau_meas is motor feedback. tau_des, when present, is the desired trajectory torque. tau_pert records perturbations when present. See csv_trajectory.py and the TMotor hardware loop and abstract controller. Source code documents the current logger convention; per-trial firmware settings and exact sample-to-command delays are not provided.",
  "limits": "5 N·m is an exact numerical reference used to describe visible plateaus in this file collection, not a verified driver limit. The reference loop first clips the controller output and then adds perturbations and motor direction before sending. A final driver command, paired unclipped/limited values and a driver saturation flag are absent from these CSV schemas. No same-row torque tracking error or physical saturation label is inferred. Separate desired-trajectory values and the model-file torque limits must not stand in for the issued drive command.",
  "reproduction": "Use Python 3 with the standard library. Download the pinned checkout or the CSVs below to their original relative paths; run python derive_leaderboard.py CHECKOUT leaderboard-runs.csv. Every source byte length and SHA-256 is checked. Compare this CSV byte-for-byte to the published table. Time statistics use the recorded per-run timestamps; no resampling or dropping of finite rows.",
